Look up a NOTIFY's send socket before freeing the string the host is in.

build_dlg_t_from_notification() parses the subscription's stored socket
string into a pkg copy, frees the copy, and then looks the socket up by the
host it parsed - which points into that copy:

	parse_phostport(tmp, &host.s, &host.len, &port, &proto);
	pkg_free(tmp);
	td->send_sock = grep_sock_info(&host, ...);

grep_sock_info() compares freed memory against the listen sockets' names, so
a NOTIFY can go out from the wrong socket, or none matches and the default
one is used. memcheck with system malloc (-X sm) reports it in the
notification process: "Invalid read at grep_sock_info, by
build_dlg_t_from_notification".

Free the copy after the lookup.

diff --git a/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/registrar_notify.c b/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/registrar_notify.c
index dcafbc8dc4..a5f11f312c 100644
--- a/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/registrar_notify.c
+++ b/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/registrar_notify.c
@@ -2949,9 +2949,10 @@ dlg_t *build_dlg_t_from_notification(reg_notification *n)
 			pkg_free(tmp);
 			goto error;
 		}
-		pkg_free(tmp);
+		/* host points into tmp */
 		td->send_sock = grep_sock_info(
 				&host, (unsigned short)port, (unsigned short)proto);
+		pkg_free(tmp);
 	}
 
 	return td;
